WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.734
-Evangeline, it is so great to see you.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.334
-It's been a long time. -It's been a while.

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:05.767
But you're allowed whenever you want --

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.667
Whenever you want to come on our show, please come on.

00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:09.100
-Thank you. -Please. Exactly. Yeah.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:12.400
I'll be visiting next time I have a great omelet.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.033
-[ Laughs ] Just come and make an omelet.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.300
-Exactly. -I just saw the movie.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.901
It's fantastic. It is a big movie.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.567
-It's a big movie.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.667
It's our biggest yet in the "Ant-Man" franchise.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.467
-Wait till you see it. It's massive.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:24.567
I was going to ask you --

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.534
-"Ant-Man and the Wasp" franchise.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:28.734
-Do you remember getting into acting

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:31.100
and your first couple of roles and, like, how that --

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.067
-I was not looking to get into acting when I got into acting.

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.567
-Really? -I was in university.

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.067
I was a broke student.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:40.367
I just needed to make some money and a job that was flexible.

00:00:40.367 --> 00:00:43.534
I had no rear window in my car.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:46.968
It was duct-taped 'cause I couldn't afford to replace it.

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:49.200
I was living on, like, peanut butter and tea.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.567
And somebody told me there's this great thing you can do.

00:00:51.567 --> 00:00:53.267
You can go on film sets. You can study all day.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:55.567
They give you free food, and they pay you for it.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:57.234
And I was like, "Fantastic!"

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:58.934
And I hooked myself up with an extra gig.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.501
And the first day on set, they were like,

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:03.634
"You, do you want to be an actor?"

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:04.901
I was like, "Nope. Don't actually.

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:06.200
I want to study my book."

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.467
They were like, "Great. You're hired."

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:09.033
And they upgraded me to actor!

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.968
-No way. -The first day on set.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.934
-See? It was just meant to be. -I just had to kiss some guy.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:16.934
-There you go. -It was on screen.

00:01:16.934 --> 00:01:18.701
On screen, of course. -Yeah, yeah, of course.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:19.868
That's all you had to do.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:21.434
-Yeah, it was just on screen. It was innocent.

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:22.534
-Yeah, it's innocent.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.167
-And then I went on to commercial work

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.934
'cause that paid a lot more.

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.734
But then that was really degrading.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.000
And then my agent was like,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.067
"Can I just send you some stuff for real roles?"

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.067
I'm like, "Dude, I don't want to be an actor.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.734
When are you gonna figure this out?"

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:37.634
He's like, "Just let me do it." And I go, "Okay, fine."

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.400
And that was in January of 2004.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.000
And in March of 2004, I was in Hawaii shooting "Lost."

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.400
-Wow. No way.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.167
And you were phenomenal in "Lost."

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.100
-And I got to replace my back windshield.

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:54.167
[ Laughter ] -All the peanut butter you want.

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:55.934
-No, actually, I got rid of that car.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:58.501
And actually, the first vehicle I bought that first season

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.701
was a 2001 Ford Escape.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.868
It was a used Ford Escape from the dealership.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.801
I am still driving that car to this day.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:06.734
-Is that right? -Yeah, yeah. 20 years later.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.434
-I love that you drive a Ford Escape.

00:02:08.434 --> 00:02:11.734
-Just a mom soccer vehicle that I've been driving for 20 years.

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.701
-I was thinking about this because "Lost"

00:02:13.701 --> 00:02:16.334
was very secretive, obviously. You're not supposed to know

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.634
what's supposed to happen, what's going to happen.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:20.701
I go -- Marvel is completely secretive.

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:22.167
So you must be good at keeping secrets.

00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:23.634
You're like, "Yeah, I'm used to this."

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.133
-I'm really not good at keeping secrets.

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:27.934
And I'm really rebellious against the whole secrets thing.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.467
'Cause I'm like, "Guys, this isn't Pentagon secrets.

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:33.300
We're not holding really, really life-changing,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.100
important information." -Yeah.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.667
-And when I was on "Lost," we were sort of

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:39.501
the beginning of that secretive thing

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:43.133
because Twitter was invented while I was shooting "Lost."

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.200
-Oh, yeah. -There was a world

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.434
before Twitter for those of you who are under 25

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.868
in the audience.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:52.033
And, so, the fans got crazy.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.734
And suddenly, there were people hungry

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:56.033
to find out what was going to happen next.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.167
So, they asked me to install a lock box

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.767
on the porch of my house

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.334
so that they could put my scripts in a lock box.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:05.467
And I was like, "There's no way. I'm not installing a lock box.

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:07.567
It's a script. You're gonna deliver it.

00:03:07.567 --> 00:03:09.501
You're gonna leave it on my porch."

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.501
And they were like, "if I do that, I will be fired.

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:13.200
I have to put it in a lock box."

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.033
-Someone's gonna leak out what's going on

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.467
with "Lost" and ruin everything.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.901
-Yeah, I never did install the lock box.

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.300
-No. -All of my scripts

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:20.767
were just hanging out on the porch when I would get home.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:21.934
-Yeah. "Come read it." Yeah.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.400
-Just free for anyone to pick up.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.834
-Yeah, your mailman's like, "I love that episode. It's great.

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.167
It's gonna be a great one for you."

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:29.234
Let's talk about "Ant-Man."

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:31.267
This is the -- This is the third one.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:32.601
-Yeah. -Right? It's massive.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.400
-Let's talk about "Ant-Man and the Wasp," shall we?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.400
-Sorry. "Ant-Man and the Wasp."

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.033
Of course. You are the Wasp.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.434
Let's talk about the Wasp and Ant-Man.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:43.968
"Quantumania." It is a massive.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:45.667
Massive, massive world.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.634
And you shrink to a very small size.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:50.100
And I'm watching this. I saw it last night.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.567
And you do this thing when you go into it,

00:03:52.567 --> 00:03:54.667
and you kind of like -- you kind of move your head.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.300
-How do you know that? -I watched it.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:57.667
-No, but can you tell?

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:59.434
I don't think you're supposed to be able to tell.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:00.634
-Yes, you have to. -Really?

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:01.701
-Paul does it, too.

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:03.234
-Yeah, 'cause the helmet has to come up.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:05.334
So you have to kind of do this, like -- like, this thing.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.734
-No. That's why I wanted to ask you about it.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.133
Paul does it, too. -It's ridiculous actually.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.300
And then when you shrink --

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.067
I can't do it sitting down. I'm gonna stand up.

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.567
Can I stand up? -Sure. Of course.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:16.801
-I'm gonna stand up.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.467
So, when I shrink, I have to do this thing

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.834
where I kind of, like, make myself get small.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.400
So I do the nod for the helmet.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:25.701
And I then I go -- Pshoo! On set.

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:28.801
But I can't do it without making the noise.

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.801
[ Laughter ] -Wait. Wait.

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:33.234
So you had to go, "Pshoo." -Yeah.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.534
So, I go -- Oh, wait. That was okay.

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:37.434
But if you stand up, I think you'll get better.

00:04:37.434 --> 00:04:39.434
Yeah, you should come around, and I can teach you.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.067
And then, actually, original "Ant-Man,"

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.868
first you had to do this, right?

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.667
You had to do this. -That's for the original.

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.234
-For the helmet. And then the shrink.

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:47.968
Pshoo! -Pshoo! Yeah, yeah.

00:04:47.968 --> 00:04:50.000
-But try not to make the noise. It's impossible.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.033
You can't do it. Ready? -Yeah.

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:54.100
-[ Squeaks ] -I had it in my head.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.300
-I did it. I did it.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:57.334
-But then, now that you're small,

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:58.901
now how do you act? Now what do you do?

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.367
You can't do the scene like this.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.067
-No. So, the first time Paul ever did this,

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:04.200
he was like -- he was like this in the scene, like,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.467
trying to get out of the scene.

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:09.167
He was crawling away, so he wasn't just hanging out

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.934
at the bottom of the scene for the rest of the scene.

00:05:11.934 --> 00:05:14.200
-So, you're doing your thing, and Paul Rudd is crawling --

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.467
-Yeah, he's crawling around behind the couch.

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:17.934
And then -- Oh, wait.

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:20.234
And then sometimes when I shrink, I'm about to fly.

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.767
That one -- That one's the most embarrassing one

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:25.501
because I have no hops.

00:05:25.501 --> 00:05:26.901
Like, none whatsoever.

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.834
So I do the helmet. -Okay. You do the h--

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:30.601
Teach me how to do it. I want to fly.

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:33.667
-And then I have to somehow shrink and fly.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.400
Fly at the same -- [ Laughter ]

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.968
-So, you -- At the same time?

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:39.701
-I don't know. -So, you're going -- Like that?

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.968
How do you make it look good, though?

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.434
-I don't know. -This is what I did.

00:05:44.434 --> 00:05:46.667
That's why I'm not in any movies.

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:48.000
You see that, and you go,

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.801
"That's not anything at all."

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.667
-You're not flying. -You make it look --

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.801
You make it look flawless. And it is amazing.

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:55.667
-Oh, it's ridiculous. -And it's so fun.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.801
And I got to say the scene that sticks out --

00:05:57.801 --> 00:06:00.133
Michelle Pfeiffer, Michael Douglas

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.934
play your parents. -[ Gasps ] Good grief.

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:03.234
-Come on. How cool it that?

00:06:03.234 --> 00:06:04.868
-I mean, it's the coolest thing ever.

00:06:04.868 --> 00:06:06.801
-And then who comes off?

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:09.667
-Dude, my 42nd birthday. -No.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.100
-No, my 42nd birthday,

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.067
I'm at a table doing a talking-head scene

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.901
with Michelle Pfeiffer, Michael Douglas,

00:06:15.901 --> 00:06:17.167
and Bill Murray.

00:06:17.167 --> 00:06:18.734
-Yeah, Bill Murray is in the movie.

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:20.300
-And I was like, "Somebody sent

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.601
the invitation to the wrong house.

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:24.334
I am not supposed to be here.

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:26.167
How did I get here? It's so cool."

00:06:26.167 --> 00:06:28.367
-No. Because you belong there. What are talking about?

00:06:28.367 --> 00:06:30.200
So you're just hanging out with those guys.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.133
-Just hanging with Michelle, Michael, and Bill.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.601
-Do they know --

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:35.901
[Valley Girl accent] "Yeah. No big deal.

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:37.100
It's just Bill.

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.634
-[Valley Girl accent] "It's my buddy, bill.

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:39.901
-That's my buddy Bill and Michelle.

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:41.934
-That is so cool. -Yeah, and --

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:43.100
-We're tight. We're tight."

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.634
-Michael. Michael, Michelle. Bill, Bill.

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:46.200
Michael, Michelle, Bill."

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:48.868 --> 00:06:50.501
Did they know it was your birthday?

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:53.067
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Actually, we were on the volume.

00:06:53.067 --> 00:06:55.267
And that's the stage with thousands of LED lights

00:06:55.267 --> 00:06:57.868
that create the Quantum Realm around us,

00:06:57.868 --> 00:06:59.901
which is really, really special.

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:02.133
-What do you see when you're in the volume?

00:07:02.133 --> 00:07:06.067
-So, what you see in the movie, we actually were in that.

00:07:06.067 --> 00:07:07.767
-Oh, so it does look like that. -It looked like that.

00:07:07.767 --> 00:07:10.067
So, instead of green screen, instead of trying to imagine

00:07:10.067 --> 00:07:11.601
all of it, it was right there.

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:14.634
I watched Krylar's ship come down from the heavens

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.133
and Bill Murray walk out of it.

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:18.234
-No way. -It was -- It was so fun!

00:07:18.234 --> 00:07:20.367
-Happy birthday to you. -I know!

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:22.267
-Come on. That's the best. -It was so good.

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:26.267
-Can we set up what's going on with "The Wasp and Ant-Man"?

00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:27.734
-Yeah, I mean, I'm going to try.

00:07:27.734 --> 00:07:29.834
I think we set it up... really well.

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:31.501
-Yeah, yeah, no. We set it up really well. Yeah.

00:07:31.501 --> 00:07:33.400
"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania."

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.834
-So, I think, in this clip, right?

00:07:36.834 --> 00:07:40.767
I think that this beautiful family nucleus that's formed now

00:07:40.767 --> 00:07:42.767
between the Langs, the Pyms, and the Van Dynes.

00:07:42.767 --> 00:07:44.234
Do you know who those people are?

00:07:44.234 --> 00:07:46.033
Do I have to explain who those people are?

00:07:46.033 --> 00:07:47.100
-No. -No, let's carry on.

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.334
They're all in the basement --

00:07:48.334 --> 00:07:50.300
-It's very family -- This movie does a great --

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.367
-Yeah, if you haven't watched the first two films,

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:53.801
then you're not my friend anyway.

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:55.601
-You don't need to watch the first two.

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:57.567
-No, I'm not gonna explain it for you. Yeah.

00:07:57.567 --> 00:08:01.267
So, we're in Hank's lab, and Cassie has opened

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:03.400
a two-way radio to the Quantum Realm.

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.000
And Janet's not very happy about this.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.300
And then things happen.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.801
-There you go. I want to show everyone a clip.

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:10.100
Here's Evangeline Lilly in

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:12.534
"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania."

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:13.834
Take a look.

00:08:13.834 --> 00:08:17.634
-So you've been studying the Quantum Realm.

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:18.734
-Mm-hmm.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.267
-Why didn't you ask me about it?

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:23.634
-I tried, Mom, a lot.

00:08:23.634 --> 00:08:25.234
You never wanted to talk about it.

00:08:25.234 --> 00:08:28.701
-Cassie's just being curious. And we gave her some pointers.

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:32.901
-This isn't exactly ant science, is it, Henry?

00:08:32.901 --> 00:08:35.467
You know how dangerous the Quantum Realm is.

00:08:35.467 --> 00:08:38.100
-We all do, Mom. Nobody's going to the Quantum Realm.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:40.667
-That's why we made this.

00:08:40.667 --> 00:08:45.667
It's like a satellite for deep space or the ocean, but...

00:08:45.667 --> 00:08:48.067
[ Whirring ] ...Quantum.

00:08:48.067 --> 00:08:49.801
-No!

00:08:49.801 --> 00:08:51.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:51.534 --> 00:08:53.534
Don't let 'em know!

00:08:53.534 --> 00:08:54.834
Evangeline Lilly.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:57.267
"Ant-Man and the Wasp: Quantumania"

00:08:57.267 --> 00:08:59.868
is in theaters and IMAX February 17th.

00:08:59.868 --> 00:09:02.400
More "Tonight Show" after the break.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.634
Stick around, everybody.

